# GitHub issue labels — mandatory on create

When the task includes **opening a GitHub issue** (issue, ticket, billet, `#NNN` visibility):

1. **Apply five label groups** on every new issue (minimum one label per group):
   - `lane:*` — `lane:a` (default ideation-to-delivery), `lane:b` (plan-incubation), `lane:c`
     (legacy retrofit), `lane:d` (post-delivery change), `lane:e` (methodology feedback)
   - `type:*` — `type:feat`, `type:fix`, `type:refactor`, `type:test`, `type:docs`, `type:chore`,
     `type:security`
   - `component:*` (one or more) — e.g. `component:admin-api`, `component:admin-ui`,
     `component:mobile`, `component:core`, `component:methodology`
   - `priority:*` — `priority:p0` (blocks release) … `priority:p3` (backlog, no urgency)
   - `status:*` — `status:needs-challenge`, `status:ready`, `status:blocked`
2. **Create with `--label` flags** on `gh issue create` — do not leave labeling for a follow-up unless the operator explicitly defers it.
3. **Verify** before reporting done: `gh issue view <N> --json labels` (or `gh issue edit` to add missing labels).
4. **Back-reference canon:** update `I-*` / `TB-*` metadata with `- **GitHub issue:** \`#NNN\``.

On Windows when `gh` is not on PATH, use `"C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe"` (see root `AGENTS.md`).

An issue reported to the operator **without labels is incomplete** — fix labels before continuing.
